Where the INTER path's port-vs-C CPU gap actually is — a three-arm decomposition.

date:    2026-09-02
host:    mac — Apple M4 Pro, 12 logical cores, aarch64-darwin.
         FOREIGN LOAD PRESENT THROUGHOUT: a sibling agent's
         `encode_backend_sweep` held ~4 cores for the whole session. See
         "IS THIS NUMBER DEFENSIBLE" below — it was checked, not assumed.
commit:  1b009a2f0bf5
cell:    gradient 256x256 qp 40 preset 8, 8-bit 4:2:0. All three arms are
         byte-identical to C at this cell.
scale:   benchmarks/perf_2026-09-02-arm-{still,videokey,inter}.tsv — paired
         interleaved, randomized order per round, 25 rounds/cell.
shares:  /usr/bin/sample, 1 ms, 12 s steady state, ~9,100-9,300 leaf samples per
         arm per side. tools/perf_profile/{prof.sh,selftime.py,classify.py}.
data:    benchmarks/perf_inter_attrib_2026-09-02.tsv

THE THREE ARMS, and why there are three. A 2-frame inter cell changes TWO things
relative to the still gate: the encoder switches from the all-intra signal
derivation to the video one, AND an inter frame appears. Measuring only "still
vs 2-frame" attributes both to "the inter path". The middle arm
(`PERF_VIDEO=1 PERF_FRAMES=1` / `SVT_AVIF=0 SVT_FRAMES=1`) is a video-mode KEY
frame and nothing else, so the two can be separated by subtraction — of
measured quantities, never a projection.

  arm        what it is                        port ms   C ms   ratio
  still      1 frame, avif still config          2.977   1.189  2.50x
  videokey   1 frame, VIDEO config              10.726   3.636  2.95x
  inter      2 frames, low-delay P              15.373   4.548  3.38x

  by subtraction:
  video config's cost ON THE KEY FRAME          7.749   2.447  3.17x
  the INTER FRAME itself                        4.647   0.912  5.10x

  Cross-check: the port harness's own FRAME_NS (9 runs, median) splits the
  2-frame encode 10.64 / 4.54 ms. The subtraction gives 10.73 / 4.65. Two
  independent methods within 1 %.

=========== FINDING 1: half the excess is the KEY frame, not the inter frame ===
Port minus C on the 2-frame cell is 10.83 ms. Split:
    still key frame          1.79 ms   17 %
    video config on the key  5.30 ms   49 %
    the inter frame          3.74 ms   35 %
That 44-52 % video-config share reproduces at EVERY cell measured — 64/128/256/
512 x presets 6/8 — and is the most stable number in the whole run. Anyone
optimising "the inter path" who starts at the motion search is starting at the
smaller half.

What the video config turns ON, per class (port ms / C ms of the 7.749 / 2.447):
    COEFF_CTX      1.406 / 0.597  (2.4x)   nz_map_ctx 0.824 ms alone
    LOOP_RESTORE   1.016 / 0.170  (6.0x)   compute_stats 0.676 + wiener_convolve 0.315
    RANGE_CODER    0.905 / 0.134  (6.7x)   OdEcEnc::normalize 0.666
    QUANT_RDOQ     0.895 / 0.551  (1.6x)   optimize_b 0.577
    CDEF           0.887 / 0.127  (7.0x)   cdef_filter_block 0.410 + cdef_find_dir 0.213
    COEFF_WRITE    0.648 / 0.176  (3.7x)   write_coeffs_txb_1d 0.619
    INTRA_PRED     0.646 / 0.060 (10.7x)   dr_predictor_edged 0.342, cfl_predict_lbd 0.123
Loop restoration and CDEF are ZERO in the still arm at preset 8 and non-zero in
the video arm on BOTH sides: the still API produces no reconstruction so the
post-filters are skipped (`EncodePipeline::with_recon_output`, the 2026-08-11
change), while a video-mode frame's recon is a reference and they must run. That
is faithful, not waste — but the port pays 6-7x C for it, and these are the SAME
kernels docs/perf-status.md's still-path SIMD queue already ranks
(`restoration::compute_stats`, `wiener_convolve_add_src`, `cdef_find_dir`,
`intra_pred::dr_predictor_edged`). **The video arm makes that existing queue
roughly twice as valuable as the still numbers suggested.**

============= FINDING 2: the inter frame is 61 % motion-search distortion ======
The port's 4.647 ms inter frame, by class (port / C):
    DISTORTION     2.824 / 0.133  (21.2x)   60.8 % of the port's inter frame
    OTHER          0.482 / 0.172   (2.8x)   10.4 %
    FWD_TXFM       0.346 / 0.142   (2.4x)    7.4 %
    LIBC_MEM       0.275 / 0.013  (21.1x)    5.9 %
    MD_DRIVER      0.270 / 0.047   (5.7x)    5.8 %
    PIPELINE       0.255 / 0.101   (2.5x)    5.5 %
    ALLOC          0.146 / 0.037   (3.9x)    3.1 %
Everything else is under 2 % or negative.

By SYMBOL, the port's inter frame:
    ms      %     symbol                                      SIMD?
    0.955  20.5   inter_me::sad::nxm_sad_kernel               SCALAR
    0.759  16.3   dsp::subpel_variance::sub_pixel_variance    SCALAR
    0.548  11.8   inter_me::sad::compute8x4_sad_kernel        SCALAR
    0.339   7.3   port_md::md_search::PlaneDistortion impls   SCALAR (plain double loops)
    0.231   5.0   intrabc::build_nmv_component_cost_table     (C has the same fn: 0.094)
    0.201   4.3   dsp::txfm_simd::neon::fdct64_x8             NEON already
    0.142   3.0   motion_est::full_pel_search                 SCALAR
"SIMD?" is by source read: none of the four scalar entries contains an
`incant!`, `#[arcane]`, `#[rite]` or `magetypes` anywhere in its file.

The same five distortion entries sum to 2.743 ms = 59.0 % of the port's inter
frame. C's whole inter frame spends 0.099 ms on the corresponding kernels:
    0.044  svt_ext_all_sad_calculation_8x8_16x16_neon
    0.035  sub_pixel_variance_w64_neon_dotprod
    0.020  svt_sad_loop_kernel_neon_dotprod
**2.743 ms against 0.099 ms — 28x.**

WHAT THAT 28x IS NOT YET SPLIT INTO, and saying so is the point. C ships NEON
and NEON-dotprod kernels for every one of these; a pure coverage gap would
plausibly account for a single-digit factor, not 28x. The rest is consistent
with the port ISSUING MORE SEARCH WORK than C — `md_search.rs` carries an MVP
scan (`best_mvp_by_distortion`), a full-pel PME (`pme_search_for_ref`) and up to
two sub-pel tree searches per reference (`md_subpel_search`,
`md_subpel_search_fixed_stage`), and none of those has ever had its call volume
compared against C's. **THAT SPLIT IS NOT MEASURED HERE.** Measuring it needs an
operation census — count SAD/variance/subpel evaluations per block on both sides
— not another profile. Do not budget a SIMD win from the table above without it:
the still path already taught this lesson once (`aom_hadamard_8x8` was 1.88 % of
p2 and delivered 1.031x because the caller's own scalar loop stayed).

===================== IS THIS NUMBER DEFENSIBLE ===============================
The box was NOT quiet. Rather than assert that the paired design handles it, the
still control re-measured 8 cells that benchmarks/perf_2026-08-13-hadamard.tsv
already carries, in this session, on this load:

  cell        08-14 ratio   this session   delta
  64  p6        1.630          1.615       -0.9 %
  64  p10       0.756          0.770       +1.9 %
  128 p6        2.386          2.396       +0.4 %
  128 p10       1.365          1.412       +3.4 %
  256 p6        3.054          3.033       -0.7 %
  256 p10       2.199          2.273       +3.4 %
  512 p6        3.058          3.024       -1.1 %
  512 p10       2.659          2.713       +2.0 %

The ABSOLUTE times did move: 512 p6 port 39.1 -> 44.0 ms and C 12.8 -> 14.6, both
about +13 %. The randomized-order paired ratio absorbed it. This is the first
time that property has been CHECKED against contention in this repo rather than
asserted. Read ratios out of this session, not absolute ms.

Profile SHARES carry the same caveat one step weaker — a share is a ratio within
one process, so contention has to bias sampling non-uniformly across symbols to
move it — but nothing here checks that directly, so treat the ms values as
share x paired-ms and the shares as +-1-2 points.

=========================== NOT MEASURED ======================================
* Any inter cell above 256x256 apples-to-apples (512x512 inter is not
  byte-identical at p8; the byte frontier ends at 256).
* More than ONE inter frame. The port refuses frame 2 outright
  ("sig_deriv_mode_decision_config_default's signals, and the reference
  statistics they read (ref_hp_percentage, ref_skip_percentage) are unported").
  Every inter number in this repo is therefore about the FIRST inter frame after
  a key frame, which is the cheapest one a GOP has.
* Any partial-SB inter cell (they panic — benchmarks/inter_completion_2026-09-02.tsv).
* The operation census that would split coverage from volume (see FINDING 2).
* 10-bit, real content, non-square dims, x86-64.
